Now I'll write the review document:
Review written to `docs/reviews/water-mains/wm-01-deg-per-day-source-verification.md`.

**Key result**: `DEG_PER_DAY = 0.986` is correct. All 3 implementations (HARES, EnergyPlus, OCHRE) agree. The value likely derives from `360/365 ≈ 0.9863` rounded to 3 significant figures — not from `360/365.25`. The `360/365.25 = 0.9856` alternative is neither more nor less correct; both are approximations. The impact of the difference is **<0.012 °C maximum** on mains temperature predictions, far below any physically meaningful threshold.
